IMPLEMENTATION (SwiftUI + @Observable + KMP facade; adaptive macOS + iOS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
New (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Charging/):
  PowershareModels.swift                 value types + pure derivations (snapshot, tones, phase)
  PowershareFormat.swift                 number/power(kW)/hours(h)/text display formatters
  PowersharePageModel.swift              @Observable model + DataSource seam + load/refresh
  PowersharePageModel.Sample.swift       Sample/Empty/Failing data-source doubles
  PowersharePage.swift                   View: header + phase switch + the two panels
  PowersharePage.Sections.swift          status panel, stat card, stop-reason panel, badge, skeleton
  PowershareRouteRegistration.swift      registers .powershare
New (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Charging/):
  PowersharePageModelTests.swift         18 XCTest cases (states/selection/derivations/format/route)
Edited:
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift             +case powershare (segment "powershare", group .vehicle, icon bolt.house.fill)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift             +PowershareRouteRegistration.registry(base:)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings     +15 keys (13 powershare.* + route.powershare + powershare.selectVehicle); reuses existing common.noData
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json          +2 rows (apple-macos + apple-ios, covered==required==21)

Data source (web parity):
  useSignalObservations -> GET /signals/observations [vehicle_id, field, since, until, limit]
  The web fires five limit=1 observation queries (PowershareStatus / PowershareType /
  PowershareStopReason / PowershareHoursLeft / PowershareInstantaneousPowerKW); the Apple
  seam aggregates them into PowershareDataSource.loadSnapshot(vehicleID:) -> PowershareSnapshot,
  bound through PowersharePageModel (no networking in the view, ADR-004).
SI discipline (ADR-005): the five signals are already materialized display values in
  signal_observations — power is delivered in kW and runtime in hours by the field itself,
  and status/type/stop-reason are text. The view renders each observation verbatim exactly
  like the web latestNumeric/latestText extractors (web fmtNumber(powerKw,2)/(hoursLeft,1));
  nothing non-SI is stored or computed. No further unit conversion applies on this page.

